  "authoritative_metadata": "manifest.json",
  "title": "The knot's count is PPADS-complete; the two-sided count is PPAD-complete",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "In the decision-tree model, finding a violated clause of the octahedral knot sphere's not-all-equal formula NAE(K_k) is PPADS^dt-complete, and finding a violated clause of NAE(K_k) together with the clauses forbidding monochromatic three-point faces is PPAD^dt-complete. Hardness composes COUNT-TFNP-20261107-001A (SINK to one-sided grid Sperner), a cyclic colour shift by -m (checked: it turns the canonical boundary into the one FLAT-STATES-20261107-001B's map expects) and that map (depth 2), which sends counterclockwise fully labelled triangles to violated lines and clockwise ones exactly to monochromatic faces (checked). Membership: the degree-3 unary Sherali-Adams certificate of COUNT-NOTE-20261107-001B, and for the two-sided count the same corner identity read as a Nullstellensatz refutation with multipliers +1 and -1. Hence, by Beame-Cook-Edmonds-Impagliazzo-Pitassi (PPADS^dt not in PPA^dt) and the characterizations PPA^dt = F2-Nullstellensatz, PPAD^dt = unary Nullstellensatz and PLS^dt = resolution width, NAE(K_k) has no polylogarithmic-degree Nullstellensatz refutation over F2 or in unary form, and the count is not in PLS^dt (its resolution width is Omega(sqrt n)).",
